	abstract = {Recent development of new procedural generation algorithms may provide an expanded generation pipeline to game programmers and designers. This work provides insight into how to combine the innovative WaveFunctionCollapse (WFC) with traditional and well-known constructive dungeon generation algorithms to create architecturally interesting and diverse environments, while discussing the strengths and weaknesses of utilizing WFC as part of the dungeon generation process and how the algorithms may interact with each other. Finally, we brieﬂy show how our generation system works and outline possible next steps for our work.},
